n{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-1)\\,i+(-3)\\,j+(2)\\,k)\\cdot ((1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (1)+(-3)\\cdot (2 t)+(2)\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =(-1)+(- 6 t)+(4 t) \\\\  & =- (2 t + 1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536002 17592186045443 true] [17592186555965 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555978 13194139536002 17592186045443 true] [17592186555965 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139536002 17592186045443 true] [17592186555965 1071 "If $f(x,y,z)=- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z$ and $r(t)=(t)\\,i+(t^{2})\\,j+(t^{2})\\,k,$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$" 13194139536002 17592186045443 true] [17592186555965 1072 #uuid "216d3edd-79b6-5b78-9d7a-c69bb1f635e7" 13194139536002 17592186045443 true] [17592186555965 1074 "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z)\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z)\\,j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- 3 x - 2 y - 3 z)\\,k \\\\  & =(-3)\\,i+(-2)\\,j+(-3)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t,y=t^{2},$ and $z=t^{2}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =(-3)\\,i+(-2)\\,j+(-3)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(1)\\,i+(2 t)\\,j+(2 t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((-3)\\,i+(-2)\\,j+(-